This licence covers the source code. The vendored datasets under data/raw/, and
the files generated from them, keep the licences of their upstreams:

- data/raw/countries.json, from mledoze/countries, is licensed ODbL-1.0. That
  is a share-alike database licence, and it reaches the files derived from it:
  src/data/graph.json, src/data/crossings.json, src/data/regions.json and
  functions/data/pairs.json. Flags carry their own terms and are excluded from
  ODbL by that project.
  https://github.com/mledoze/countries

- data/raw/countries-110m.json, from topojson/world-atlas, is licensed ISC and
  derives from Natural Earth, which places its data in the public domain.
  https://github.com/topojson/world-atlas

See the Data section of README.md for what each file is and why it is vendored.
